From 51c19315ff8e77f22711e78753af96affa00a029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:10:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 40/51] coh: per-thread split of the work a Megalon-hwcc
 all-HWcc also does (build 75)

rackobj::GetThreadAnchor (= shim v3 AnchorSnap, field order fixed): read
lookup / NR anchor work of the sampled read sections (excluded from check
since 74), rseq_ns_sampled = seqlock version reads whose time is in check
(RSeqBegin of read_seq_start minus its spin, attempts outside (A);
RSeqRetry of read_seq_end of accepted sections), write lookup / NR anchor
work (excluded from wstart), wseq_ns = final attempt's WSeqBegin (inside
wstart), wseq_end_ns = WSeqEnd (inside wflush). c3.cc hooks are active only
while the callers set the thread-local flags. CohSnap unchanged.
Observation only, no protocol change. object-test logs per-section values
(ANCHOR-PER-SECTION) for comparing the megalon and hwcc flavors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
